e('Inode count is fixed at `mkfs` time, so millions of tiny files can exhaust inodes before space.','Each block group reserves an inode table. At a fixed filesystem size, tiny files can exhaust available inodes before data space; growing the filesystem can add groups and inodes.','Growth can increase inode count.',ext)
